+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|                    ADD / SUB CALCULATOR CORE                |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+

  SUPPLY (5V REGULATED)
  ---------------------
  [BAT+]----[VREG 5V]------------------+----------------------+
                                       |                      |
                                      [RPD] 10kΩ             [RPD] 10kΩ
                                       |                      |
  [BAT-]-------------------------------+----------------------+
                                       |                      |
                                      GND                    GND


  INPUTS
  ------
  BTN_OP   (momentary)  POT_CTRL (10kΩ linear)

  BTN_OP:
    [BTN_OP]----+------------------------[RPU] 10kΩ----+---- 5V
                |                                      |
               [C1] 100nF                             [Q1] NPN
                |                                      |
               GND                                   NODE_OP
                |
    (RC debounce + NPN to create clean logic pulse)

  POT_CTRL:
    [POT] top ---- 5V
    [POT] wiper --+----> NODE_ANALOG
    [POT] bottom - GND

    NODE_ANALOG → feeds simple 4‑level comparator ladder:

    NODE_ANALOG --[R1]--+--[R2]--+--[R3]--+--[R4]-- GND
                         |        |        |
                        [Q2]     [Q3]     [Q4]
                         |        |        |
                       BIT0     BIT1     BIT2   (3‑bit operand)


  CORE REGISTERS (4‑bit ACCUMULATOR)
  ----------------------------------
  ACC0, ACC1, ACC2, ACC3 implemented as D flip‑flops:

    BIT0 ----> [FA0] ----> [FF0] ----> ACC0
    BIT1 ----> [FA1] ----> [FF1] ----> ACC1
    BIT2 ----> [FA2] ----> [FF2] ----> ACC2
    0   ----> [FA3] ----> [FF3] ----> ACC3

  Each [FFx] is built from discrete transistors:

    [FFx]:
      [Q5] NPN, [Q6] NPN, [R5–R8] forming master–slave latch
      CLK from NODE_OP pulse


  ADD / SUB SELECT
  ----------------
  MODE_SUB toggle switch:

    [SW_MODE]----[RMS] 10kΩ---- 5V
                 |
                [Q7] NPN → NODE_MODE (HIGH = SUB, LOW = ADD)

  TWO’S COMPLEMENT FOR SUB:
    BIT0..BIT2 → XOR with NODE_MODE:

      BITn ----[Q8/Q9 pair]----> BITn' (inverted when SUB)
      CARRY_IN = NODE_MODE (1 for SUB, 0 for ADD)

    FA0–FA3 are full adders built from discrete gates:

      [FAx]:
        SUM  = A XOR B XOR Cin
        Cout = majority(A,B,Cin)
      Implemented with:
        - XOR: 4 × NPN + resistor network
        - AND/OR: 2 × NPN + resistors


  CLOCK / OP PULSE
  ----------------
  NODE_OP (from Q1) → CLK line:

    NODE_OP ----[RCLK] 1kΩ----> all FFx CLK inputs


  OUTPUT / DISPLAY
  ----------------
  ACC0..ACC3 → LED bar or 7‑segment driver:

    ACC0 ----[RLED0] 1kΩ----> LED0 → GND
    ACC1 ----[RLED1] 1kΩ----> LED1 → GND
    ACC2 ----[RLED2] 1kΩ----> LED2 → GND
    ACC3 ----[RLED3] 1kΩ----> LED3 → GND

  Optional overflow LED:

    CARRY_OUT_FA3 ----[RLED_OV] 1kΩ----> LED_OV → GND

+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| OPERATION                                                   |
| - POT sets 3‑bit operand (0–7) via comparator ladder        |
| - MODE_SUB selects ADD or SUB (two’s complement)            |
| - BTN_OP pulse clocks operand into accumulator via FAs      |
| - LEDs show current 4‑bit accumulator value                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
